{"id":"4e3aa745a4d7cc44","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-binary-reduction-decidability.md","title":"Many-One Reduction Preserves Decidability Downward","display":"thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-decidability — Many-One Reduction Preserves Decidability Downward","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-binary-reduction-decidability","aliases":["73-thm-binary-reduction-decidability","73-thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-decidability"],"display":"thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-decidability — Many-One Reduction Preserves Decidability Downward","depends_on":["[[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]]","[[73-df-dtm-language-decision]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-binary-reduction-decidability"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-binary-reduction-decidability</span><span>73-thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-decidability</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-decidability — Many-One Reduction Preserves Decidability Downward"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64d902370bb28edb\" href=\"?note=64d902370bb28edb\" title=\"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction\">73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"004d4e2ba3fdd14e\" href=\"?note=004d4e2ba3fdd14e\" title=\"73-df-dtm-language-decision\">73-df-dtm-language-decision</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_m\">\\(\\leq_m\\)</span> (computable many-one reducibility, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"64d902370bb28edb\" href=\"?note=64d902370bb28edb\" title=\"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction\">73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\">\\(\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\\)</span> (decidable binary languages, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"004d4e2ba3fdd14e\" href=\"?note=004d4e2ba3fdd14e\" title=\"73-df-dtm-language-decision\">73-df-dtm-language-decision</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}decidability}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\n\\longrightarrow A\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}decidability}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\n\\longrightarrow A\\in\\mathsf{DEC}_{\\mathbf 2}\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Compute a total reduction witness <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span> and run a decider for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B\">\\(B\\)</span> on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f(x)\">\\(f(x)\\)</span>. The defining biconditional for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_m\">\\(\\leq_m\\)</span> gives the right answer, and totality of both computations gives halting on every input.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","status":"resolved","id":"64d902370bb28edb","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","locatio